                    {
                        "form_id": "b931d8da-6284-4b66-afa9-f8dad8de06e2",
                        "entry_id": "7a08b413-ec06-3b2a-bde4-e0e73acb8c7a",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "steelmanned"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b42f564e-b4b2-3c02-9b1c-f71be6032c6b",
                        "entry_id": "7a08b413-ec06-3b2a-bde4-e0e73acb8c7a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To repair flaws in an argument before analyzing it critically; to refute or to weaken the force of a stronger version of an argument than what was actually given."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "44988129-5758-406f-ae50-43a2ae15c1dc",
                                "sense_id": "b42f564e-b4b2-3c02-9b1c-f71be6032c6b",
                                "text": "I don't agree with the argument, because of 4. If I were to steelman it, which I may try but after work or maybe during lunch, I would first try to make it impervious to this assault:"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "af629328-76b0-477d-9b13-2f9b6035b9a3",
                                "sense_id": "b42f564e-b4b2-3c02-9b1c-f71be6032c6b",
                                "text": "It is possible that while preparing for the talk I will manage to convince myself that the problem is in fact resolved or dissolved. In that case I will treat you to my best steelmanning of the problem, and its resolution."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "78b93d75-4dee-4fb0-a95c-53ae89d47998",
                                "sense_id": "b42f564e-b4b2-3c02-9b1c-f71be6032c6b",
                                "text": "Perhaps the argument should be steelmanned in that we should generally avoid using algorithms which are so complex that they aren't glass boxes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "36a0ac79-231a-4a52-9ce4-587b37a4e673",
                                "sense_id": "b42f564e-b4b2-3c02-9b1c-f71be6032c6b",
                                "text": "And America would benefit if our culture of argument elevated the opposite approach, steel-manning, “the art of addressing the best form of the other person’s argument, even if it’s not the one they presented.” […] Coming full circle to our NPR host’s project, Messinger argues that “steelmanning makes you a better person."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
